    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7b578c3_15f73c05",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-26T02:24:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, if I understand this correctly, the problem is that on lid close, EC kills the backlight enable without giving AP a chance to do the proper sequencing. I would think that this is a problem on most(all?) devices since HOOK_LID_CHANGE is triggered as soon as lid is opened/closed. In my opinion, the right thing to do would be in backlight_lid.c: https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/common/backlight_lid.c?type\u003dcs\u0026q\u003df:ec+GPIO_ENABLE_BACKLIGHT\u0026g\u003d0\u0026l\u003d30\n\n1. Check if lid is open --\u003e If yes, enable backlight right away.\n2. Check if lid is closed --\u003e If yes, schedule a deferred call after x seconds and then pull the backlight off.\n\nThis will ensure that the backlight gets turned off in case the AP fails to do itself for any reason on lid close.",
      "parentUuid": "63d73333_b8ad286a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "c94492842b2f239dd1a253a5722e6c51410880b5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
